# VS Code patches

`lib/vscode` is a git submodule. DroidLabX changes belong in `patches/` (see `patches/series`).

```text
quilt new {name}.diff          # or reuse an existing patch
quilt add lib/vscode/path/file # MUST run before editing that file
# edit the file
quilt refresh                  # fold the diff into the patch
```

- Comment the patch: why it exists and how to see the behavior.
- User-visible patch behavior gets an e2e under `test/e2e`.
- Do not commit submodule dirty files as a substitute for a quilt patch.
- Prefer deleting unused workbench chrome in the patch over hiding it from Android.

```text
# ❌ BAD
edit lib/vscode/... then git add lib/vscode

# ✅ GOOD
quilt add lib/vscode/... && edit && quilt refresh
```
